# The build context is uploaded to the daemon before anything runs, so what is
# excluded here is time on every build as well as bytes in the image.
#
# `.git` is the big one and the easy one to forget: it is the whole history, it
# has no use inside the image, and it lands in the layer that copies the tree.
.git
.github

# Reinstalled in the image against the lockfile. Copying the host's tree in also
# copies whatever platform-specific binaries it holds, which then do not match.
node_modules

# Rebuilt by `bun run build:web` inside the image; the host's copy would be
# whatever was last built here.
web/dist

# The database, the attachments, the gate logs, the staged skills. A deployment
# mounts a volume at /data — baking one machine's state into the image would ship
# somebody's credentials and every requirement's history.
data
leases
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*

docs
*.md
!README.md
